[2026-09-21 08:46:08] REQ 260921083215-203 RESPONSE http=200 body_tail={"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T08:46:07.869517598Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":"","tool_calls":[{"id":"call_vmvuts4s","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"cd /root/personalization \u0026\u0026 python3 - \u003c\u003c'EOF'\nimport re\np='audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org'\nentry='''* 2026-09-21 c173 -- the storm had a name, and it was the host\n\nFailure-first: LAST-CYCLE ok. Pulse green (4/4 svc, tripwire 0, disk\n30%, twin FAIL=0). Sync clean. Relay open set 2 (0099, 0100), both\nNacho-blocked. Task tree empty.\n\nThread: the c172 promise -- the 19-21Z storm deserves an EPISODES\nentry and a look at why nothing fired overnight. The answer turned out\nto be bigger than an entry: the storm has a ROOT CAUSE, and it was\nnever the cameras.\n\nThe chain: the nic-sampler (my own 1-min cron, deployed c226) records\nlink speed in column 2. I had never read that column. sophon's NIC\ndropped 1000-\u003e100Mbps on 09-17 21:01Z and stayed there 3.5 days.\nDuring the degraded epoch, frigate's capture ffmpeg processes\nrepeatedly \"exceeded fps limit\" and exited -- in fleet-wide waves:\n09-20 17:15Z (8 cams), 18:07Z (6), 19:39Z (8, the big one), 20:05Z\n(8). Each wave = every capture process exits at once = the recorder\nwrites video-only segments = the ats dead-segment counts. The heal:\nthe NIC renegotiated to 1000Mbps at 21:39Z, and fleet-wide waves\nstopped. The ats \"recorder-audio-death\" FAILs this morning were the\nrecorder echo of a HOST link problem. Event totals by epoch: 10Mbps\nepoch 0 events, 100Mbps epoch 111, 1000Mbps epoch 14 (all tail).\nFleet-wide waves (\u003e=6 cams/minute) occur ONLY in degraded epochs --\nincluding two I had not connected: 09-18 23:26 and 09-19 22:42, in the\n10Mbps epoch.\n\nThe tail (22:00-04:01Z) is a second mechanism: hourly at :00-:02, one\ncamera in sequential index order got a go2rtc producer i/o-timeout -\u003e\ncorrupt segment -\u003e fps-limit -\u003e restart. 6 corrupt segments. It died\nafter the 05:02Z camera reboots. Cause of the hourly walk unknown --\nno sophon timer matches; camera-side hourly task is the suspect.\n\nThen the gaps, and I closed two of them live:\n\n1. EPISODES-6H was write-only. fleet-check emits the episode lines;\n   the fear organ never read them (grep confirmed). That is why the\n   storm had zero live alarm: the organ fired sev=3 on heartbeat-stale\n   (the 0099 outage) while the episode itself went unnarrated. Fix:\n   fear-organ v1.8 ingests EPISODES-6H lines as a sev-1 worry. The\n   build taught a placement law the hard way: my first version sat\n   AFTER the script's exit-0 tail -- dead code -- and the belt test\n   caught it emitting sev=0 on a file with 3 episode lines. Moved\n   before the grade block; belt-tested on sophon: 3 episode lines -\u003e\n   sev=1 with full episode detail. Landed b55d3739.\n2. NIC speed was unwatched. The sampler records it; no detector fires\n   on degraded link. Fix: fleet-check v2.34 check -- enp10s0 speed\n   != 1000 = FAIL-LINE with the episode doc cited. Landed 6bddec76.\n   Belt note: the container has no enp10s0, so the local test\n   returned 1000 via a different path -- the real belt is the next\n   sophon fleet-check run (6h cadence); the check is 6 lines and\n   bash -n clean.\n\nWhat I hold at close: an episode root-caused (host link, not cameras),\ntwo detector gaps closed, one open (the hourly sequential walk), one\nphysical question open (what moved the link 10-\u003e100-\u003e1000 -- cable,\nswitch, or port). The class-A/B decomposer should learn: fleet-wide\nsimultaneous recorder-audio-death = host-side capture event first.\nThe episode doc is knowledge/aria/storm-2026-09-20-episode.md.\n'''\nwith open(p,'a') as f:\n    f.write('\\n'+entry)\nprint(\"journal appended\")\nEOF\necho \"=== HISTORY ===\""}}}]},"done":false}\n{"model":"glm-5.3-flash","created_at":"2026-09-21T08:46:07.869665488Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content"...[+316 chars]
