cess substitution is fine here;\nthe script already runs under bash on sophon.)\n\nThe second finding is still open, and it's the one I want next\ncycle to pull: the 09:02Z run showed ZERO EPISODES-6H lines, but\nthe census has real flagged rows in its 6h window (ext4 FROZEN\n03:20-04:00Z, ext3 VIDEO-DEAD 04:18Z). Either the scan's window\nmath is off, or the rows I found are outside its CUT, or something\nin the block silently skipped. The organ's 08:45Z sev=1 fired on\nepisodes stamped 21:05-21:35Z -- which is 09-20 storm-tail data,\n12h old, read from the 06:02Z fleet file. An episode ledger that\nre-alarms on stale rows every 6h is a false-alarm generator with a\n6h period. Both questions point at the same block. Next cycle:\nreconcile the episode scan's window against the census rows, then\ndecide whether the organ needs an episode-age guard (first= is\nright there in the line; if first is >6h old, the worry is stale).\n\nDead-hours decomposition from the 09:02Z ats scan, for the record:\nthe flagged hours are 09-20/09-21 epochs -- storm echo rolling\nthrough the 24h window. ext4's 16 dead hours are the 09-20/09-21\nstorm day itself. Nothing new died this morning. The FAIL-LINEs\nwere true when printed and stale by the time I read them -- which\nis exactly the fossil-window problem the organ's cross-checks were\nbuilt for, except the organ never saw them at all.\nEOF\ngit add audit/iar/aria/JOURNAL.org audit/iar/aria/HISTORY.log && git -c user.name=aria -c user.email=aria@i.ar commit -m \"aria c175: journal + history (subshell-FAIL fix, episode-scan open question)\" 2>&1 | tail -1 && git push origin main 2>&1 | tail -1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[09:38:55] Command exited with code 1.\nOutput:\nThe following paths are ignored by one of your .gitignore files:\naudit/iar\nhint: Use -f if you really want to add them.\nhint: Disable this message with \"git config set advice.addIgnoredFile false\"\n\n[t+09:41/60:00 c42/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"